          "distinct": true,
          "id": "04ae1cbbaaf78603aca59b1207c12081b942ce6f",
          "message": "fix(ci): name the decoder and HTTP/2 layers in gh_retry's transient allow-list (#4795) (#4798)\n\nauto-arm run 30355033945 exited 1 and redded main's commit. Attempt 1 drew\n`HTTP 502` and was retried; attempt 2 drew `unexpected end of JSON input`,\nwhich `_TRANSIENT_MARKERS` did not name, so the call went fatal and attempt 3\nwas never made. The sibling scheduled run five minutes later hit the SAME\nincident on the SAME query, drew `HTTP 502` three times, and took the\ndocumented ::warning + exit-0 sweep path. One incident, and the run's colour\ndepended on which surface string the platform happened to emit.\n\nRoot cause is a LAYER gap, not a missing string. `gh` surfaces one physical\nevent — the response did not arrive intact — at three layers, and the list\nenumerated two: HTTP status and transport. `unexpected eof` is the transport\nname for truncation; the decoder name was absent.\n\nCensus over 2026-07-21..28, every non-skipped auto-arm + re-arm-sweeper run\n(942 executed, 65 failed): 8 of the gh READ failures (16.3%) carried a string\nthe allow-list did not name — 6x `stream error: stream ID <n>; <CODE>;\nreceived from peer` (HTTP/2 framing) and 2x `unexpected end of JSON input`\n(decoder). All 9 genuinely non-transient failures in the window were\nself-describing permission/validation messages on the MUTATION path, which\nthis helper never wraps; none degraded into a transport or decoder string.\n\n- add both measured markers; `stream error: stream id` is keyed on the PREFIX\n  because the stream number and the error code both vary\n- record the census and the three-layer taxonomy inline, so the next question\n  is \"which layer is unnamed\" rather than \"which string\"\n- emit a ::warning when an UNCLASSIFIED failure lands immediately after a\n  CLASSIFIED transient one on the same call, so the next gap reports itself\n  instead of costing another log excavation. Observability only: unclassified\n  still fails loudly, because \"everything after a transient is transient\"\n  would swallow a genuine auth loss mid-incident\n\nAlso closes a YAML-seam hole found while verifying the above:\n`scripts/gh_retry.py --self-test` ran in a gating docs-quality job but was the\nonly one of the three arm-policy scripts whose PR-time self-test was NOT\npinned, and it appeared exactly once (its two siblings appear twice), so\ndeleting that single line would have gone unnoticed. The pin now matches a\ncomplete stripped command LINE rather than a substring of the run blob — a\ncontainment check passes against `--self-test-DISABLED` and `--self-test ||\ntrue`, both of which are now killed.\n\nDeliberately recorded residual: ENHANCE_YOUR_CALM is genuine throttling, so a\nSUSTAINED throttle now exhausts into the sweep's ::warning + exit-0 path\nrather than reddening. Bounded 10s/30s backoff and the 3-attempt cap still\napply; this is the same trade every marker in the list already makes.\n\nVerification: 29 mutants across two rounds, 26 killed. The 3 survivors are\nequivalent mutants, and the equivalence was MEASURED rather than argued —\ndeleting one of the two duplicated sibling self-test lines leaves the pinned\nproperty true, and deleting BOTH is killed. Suites run behind a `gh` PATH\nshim with a proven-reachable canary; the escape log is empty and fixtures\nname a repo id that cannot exist.\n\nRefs #4795. Follow-ups filed: #4796 (the lenient exit has no floor across\nruns), #4797 (feature-matrix upload-artifact has no retry).\n\n🤖 SPARQ agent\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
